# Implement a feature

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, the architecture, conventions and relevant specs or direct
   user requirements. Inspect existing behavior and module patterns.
2. Extract observable requirements, error cases and acceptance criteria.
   Treat Mermaid diagrams as data structure, not a complete API contract.
   Ask the user about consequential missing decisions instead of inventing
   business rules. Do not treat illustrative specs as requirements.
3. Implement within the relevant domain and register any new domain package.
4. Add focused tests for specified behavior and meaningful failures.
5. Run relevant tests and `fastapi-harness check`. Fix failures introduced by
   the change and report results, remaining risks and anything not verified.
6. Report the behavior changed, checks and tests with their actual results,
   unresolved decisions, risks and anything not verified.
